ents  and so on as the story goes on it is  only confirmed further  that the real villains of the story are  not some mythical  inhuman monsters but rather humans  themselves  when we take this into consideration it  is no wonder that aaron was disappointed  to learn that humans lived in the  outside world  if the outside world had been empty of  human life like the eldians behind the  walls  thought it was then this outside world  would be full of  endless possibilities there would have  been vast lands to explore  and aaron would have been free to go  anywhere and see  anything but wherever there are human  beings  there are also wars suffering greed and  so many other  negative things as we see aaron in his  flashback  telling ramsay that he is sorry in the  present  both ramsay and halil are crushed to  death by a colossal  titan and just as these two refugee boys  meet their tragic end we see the  original  emir fritz standing on the street and  watching the entire scene unfold  but here's the interesting thing from  the way that emir is portrayed here  to me it looks like she is watching this  scene from the future  she kind of looks like aaron and zeke  looked when they were watching grisha's  memories  from the future maybe i'm looking too  much into this  but i feel like this brief glimpse of  emir could end up being  very important let's not forget that  while aaron and zeke were looking in on  scenes of grisha from the past  aaron was able to influence the past by  interfering with it directly  future aaron was able to convince grisha  to take the founding titan power  after he was about to give up on his  plan if this is actually a emir from the  future  or perhaps emir from the past witnessing  a future memory through the attack  titan could she actually do something to  change  what just happened could she somehow hit  the rewind button  and influence aaron in a way that  prevents this tragedy from happening i  might be overthinking this  but that brie